    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p1_b48",
      "text": "Promptable segmentation models such as SAM and Med-\nSAM provide a promising way to extract lesion regions\nthrough spatial prompts [5], [6], [18]. Recent studies have fur-\nther explored medical SAM adaptation from multiple perspec-\ntives, including uncertainty-guided multi-prompt adaptation,\nSAM-based semi-supervised decoding, lightweight modality-\ndecoupled adaptation, and gaze-assisted prompting [19]\u2013[22].\nHowever, their effectiveness still depends heavily on whether\nthe provided prompts can reliably indicate the lesion area.\nManual prompts are costly, while automatically generated\n",
